689 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 524 0 R
/E (Walk into any conversation about how men can "attract women" and you'll find two camps shouting past each other. One camp says it's all about tricks ? the right opening line, the right amount of eye contact, the right way to seem uninterested so she chases you. The other camp says there's no such thing as attraction skill at all ? you either have it or you don't, and trying is embarrassing. Both camps are wrong, and both are wrong for the same reason: they treat attraction as some thing that happens to a woman, engineered by a man, rather than something that happens between two people who are both choosing, the whole time, whether to keep choosing each other. That distinction is the entire spine of this book. A woman deciding whether she's interested in you is not a lock waiting for the right combination. She is a person running the same kind of evaluation you'd run on anyone .i.e. is this person safe, interesting, kind, capable, funny, respectful than you'd guess, because she has more practice. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
690 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 524 0 R
/E (Most women navigate far more romantic attention than most men realize, from a much younger age, which means the average woman has an extremely well-calibrated radar for performance versus authenticity. Scripts, lines, and "techniques" tend to trip that radar, not bypass it.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
