/P 525 0 R
/E (So why does so much popular advice still sell tricks? Because tricks are easy to package and sell, and because a trick that "works" once is easy to mistake for a system. If you say a clever line to ten women, one of them was already inclined to like you for unrelated reasons, and you'll remember that one success and credit the line. This is survivorship bias, and an entire industry is built on it.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
