722 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 529 0 R
/E (Chapter Twenty- before we get there, you need a clear line drawn in the sand between manipulation and attraction, Attraction is what happens when someone freely, knowingly decides they like being around you, based on an accurate picture of who you are. Manipulation is what happens when someone is maneuvered into a feeling or a decision using a false picture , false interest, false scarcity, false vulnerability, exploited insecurity  that you constructed on purpose. The outcome can look similar from the outside for a while. A manipulated "yes" and a freely given "yes" can sound the same in the moment. But they are not the same thing, and they do not hold up the same way over time, because one of them is built on accurate information and the other is built on a lie that eventually surfaces.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
