735 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 531 0 R
/E (Here's an uncomfortable but useful reframing: the question "how do I attract her" is usually asked one step too late. The more useful question, asked earlier, is "what kind of life am I building, and is it one worth inviting someone into?" This isn't a platitude. It's practical, because almost everything down stream in this book  confidence, conversation, what you talk about on a date, what you have to offer emotionally  flows from whether you actually have a life. Men who are anxious and try-hard in dating are very often men who have made the person they're pursuing the emotional center of their week, with nothing else pulling equal weight. That imbalance is felt by the other person almost immediately, even if they can't name it. It reads as neediness, and neediness is one of the most reliable attraction- killers there is not because wanting connection is shameful, but because a life with no other center of gravity puts enormous, unfair pressure on one relationship to hold everything up.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
