/T (Choose three qualities you already possess and three you want to strengthen. Then translate each quality into observable behavior. 'Confident' might become 'state my preference without apologizing for it.' 'Warm' might become 'ask one follow-up question and actually listen to the answer.' 'Interesting' might become 'maintain hobbies and projects that I would pursue even if nobody noticed.' The point is to build traits through evidence rather than labels.)
/E (Choose three qualities you already possess and three you want to strengthen. Then translate each quality into observable behavior. 'Confident' might become 'state my preference without apologizing for it.' 'Warm' might become 'ask one follow-up question and actually listen to the answer.' 'Interesting' might become 'maintain hobbies and projects that I would pursue even if nobody noticed.' The point is to build traits through evidence rather than labels.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [3]
>>
