/T (Chasing often begins as a response to uncertainty: one message goes unanswered, so another is sent; a conversation becomes quieter, so the person tries harder; interest feels ambiguous, so every small signal is analyzed. A better response is to return to your actual life. Finish the workday. Meet a friend. Exercise. Read. Continue the plans you already had. If the conversation resumes, engage normally.)
/E (Chasing often begins as a response to uncertainty: one message goes unanswered, so another is sent; a conversation becomes quieter, so the person tries harder; interest feels ambiguous, so every small signal is analyzed. A better response is to return to your actual life. Finish the workday. Meet a friend. Exercise. Read. Continue the plans you already had. If the conversation resumes, engage normally.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [7]
