796 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 538 0 R
/E (Suppose a first date has gone well for ninety minutes. Anxiety may tell you to keep extending the evening because ending it might reduce momentum. Restraint says something simpler: 'I've had a good time. I'd like to see you again.' Then you leave. There is no hidden message. You are allowing the positive experience to stand on its own.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
797 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 538 0 R
/E (Early connection naturally contains unknowns. You do not yet know someone's full history, ambitions, fears, friendships, or private habits. There is no need to reveal everything immediately, and there is no need to hide everything either. Mystery is simply the space created by a relationship unfolding over time.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
798 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 538 0 R
/E (Restraint is the ability to let that process happen without forcing it. You can answer honestly without telling the entire story. You can show interest without demanding constant contact. You can end a good conversation before it becomes exhausted. You can keep parts of your life private because they are yours, not because privacy is a weapon.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [10]
>>
