/P 540 0 R
/E (You send a message and receive' haha yeah' in response. That message alone tells you very little. Look at the broader pattern. Has she been engaged? Does she make plans? Has the conversation usually had substance? If the pattern remains distant over time, reduce your effort. If normal engagement returns, there was no need to invent a crisis.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
815 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 540 0 R
/E (A single smile, short reply, delayed message, or intense look is weak evidence. Repeated behavior across different settings is stronger. Social awareness improves when you stop treating every small event as a coded message about your worth.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
816 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 540 0 R
/E (Look for congruence: does her behavior generally match her words? Does she voluntarily continue conversations? Does she ask questions, remember details, initiate sometimes, make time, or suggest another meeting? These are not a mathematical formula for attraction. They are pieces of context.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
817 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 540 0 R
/E (People become tired, busy, distracted,anxious, excited,or preoccupied for reasons that have nothing to do with you. Someone can be quieter today because work went badly. Someone can be enthusiastic one week and exhausted the next. A socially intelligent person leaves room for those possibilities instead of immediately choosing the explanation that confirms his fear or hope.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [11]
>>
