828 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 542 0 R
/E (Use a simple rhythm: notice, respond, deepen. Notice something she says. Respond with your own reaction, opinion, or related story. Then deepen the topic with a natural question. This makes the exchange reciprocal.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
829 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 542 0 R
/E (For example: 'You said you changed careers last year.' Notice. 'That sounds risky; I respect people who can make that kind of decision.' Respond. 'What finally made you decide it was time?' Deepen. The conversation now contains observation, personal contribution, and curiosity rather than a sequence of interview prompts.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
