831 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 542 0 R
/E (People often remember conversations because of emotional texture :a surprising observation, a funny mistake, an unusually specific story, a moment of honest disagreement, or a shared discovery. None of those requires a scripted line.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
832 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 542 0 R
/E (A conversation becomes flat when one person acts like an interviewer. Questions are useful, but they should create movement rather than extract information. If she says she loves traveling, you can ask where she has been, but you can also contribute: 'I love traveling, but I'm terrible at planning. I once booked a place because the photos looked perfect and discovered it was basically a construction site.' Now she has something to react to.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [9]
>>
