/P 548 0 R
/E (A healthy connection contains some reciprocity. You initiate sometimes; she initiates sometimes. You suggest plans; she makes time or proposes alternatives. You show curiosity; she gives you something to be curious about. The exact balance will vary, but a persistent one-sided pattern is information.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
887 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 548 0 R
/E (Step back when invitations are repeatedly declined without alternatives, when responses remain consistently minimal, when you are always the one initiating, or when someone clearly states a boundary. Stepping back is not a punishment. It is the decision to stop pushing where there is insufficient mutual interest.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [10]
>>
