955 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 557 0 R
/T (Here's a fact most dating advice skips entirely: the average woman, especially an attractive or socially active one, has fielded a lot of romantic attention by the time you meet her. She has options. She has almost certainly been on the receiving end of copy-paste messages, recycled lines, and men who were more interested in "a girlfriend" as a category than in her specifically. Understanding this isn't about intimidation. it's the single most useful piece of context for why generic approaches fail and specific, attentive ones don't. "Understanding her" doesn't mean decoding her like a puzzle. It means doing the ordinary, unglamorous work of actually getting to know a specific person ,Nher actual sense of humor, not a generic one; what she's stressed about this week; what she's proud of; what kind of attention she actually enjoys versus tolerates. This is slower than a script, and that's the point ? it can't be faked at scale, which is exactly why it stands out.)
/E (Here's a fact most dating advice skips entirely: the average woman, especially an attractive or socially active one, has fielded a lot of romantic attention by the time you meet her. She has options. She has almost certainly been on the receiving end of copy-paste messages, recycled lines, and men who were more interested in "a girlfriend" as a category than in her specifically. Understanding this isn't about intimidation. it's the single most useful piece of context for why generic approaches fail and specific, attentive ones don't. "Understanding her" doesn't mean decoding her like a puzzle. It means doing the ordinary, unglamorous work of actually getting to know a specific person ,Nher actual sense of humor, not a generic one; what she's stressed about this week; what she's proud of; what kind of attention she actually enjoys versus tolerates. This is slower than a script, and that's the point ? it can't be faked at scale, which is exactly why it stands out.)
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [3]
