<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 561 0 R
/E (You might have heard dating advice that sorts women into two types:- the ones who care about connection, and the "materialistic" ones who care about gifts and being taken out. That split doesn't hold up, and it's worth saying plainly why: thoughtful gestures aren't a special category of thing that only some women want. They're simply one of the ordinary languages people use to feel cared for  and most people respond to some version of it, in some proportion, alongside everything else in this book. The real variable isn't "which type of girl is this." It's thoughtfulness versus generic spending. A $200 bouquet chosen because it's expensive says less than a $15 bouquet of the specific flower she once mentioned liking. A dinner at the "right" restaurant because it photographs well says less than a dinner somewhere you found because you remembered she loves a specific cuisine. Money can signal effort, but it's a weak signal on her.)
/Pg 54 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
