<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 568 0 R
/E (Two traits show up again and again in attraction research and in plain observation: a good sense of humor, and the willingness to be a little vulnerable. They work for the same underlying reason  both signal that you're comfortable enough with yourself to not need to perform constant composure. Humor that works is usually about noticing, not memorizing. Observational, situational humor  reacting genuinely to what's actually happening  lands better than rehearsed jokes, because it proves you're actually present rather than running material. Vulnerability, in small, appropriate doses, builds trust faster than any amount of polish. Admitting you're nervous, admitting you don't know something, telling a story that isn't flattering to you, these signal security, not weakness, because only someone reasonably secure can afford to admit them. The key word is appropriate: heavy emotional disclosure on  build with trust.)
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
