/T (Confidence is one of the most requested and least understood traits in this entire subject. Here's a working definition that actually holds up: confidence is comfort with the possibility of rejection. Arrogance is the belief that you're owed acceptance. They are frequently confused because both can look bold from a distance  but only one of them is actually attractive, and it isn't the one built on entitlement.)
/E (Confidence is one of the most requested and least understood traits in this entire subject. Here's a working definition that actually holds up: confidence is comfort with the possibility of rejection. Arrogance is the belief that you're owed acceptance. They are frequently confused because both can look bold from a distance  but only one of them is actually attractive, and it isn't the one built on entitlement.)
/Pg 62 0 R
