1071 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 573 0 R
/E (Ask directly, ask specifically, and ask in a way that makes saying no easy and comfortable for her. Those three rules cover almost everything. Directly means saying what you mean: "Would you like to get dinner with me Friday?" beats "We should hang out sometime" ? the vague version puts the work of clarifying your intentions back on her, which isn't fair to ask of her. Specifically means offering an actual plan like a place, a rough time  rather than an open-ended "let me know when you're free." A concrete plan is easier to say yes to and easier to say no to; ambiguity just creates friction in both directions. Comfortably means your tone and body language should make clear that a "no" won't cost her anything  no awkwardness, no guilt, no change in how you treat her afterward. That ease is itself attractive, because it signals real confidence rather than a hidden agenda riding on her answer.)
/Pg 66 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
