<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 575 0 R
/E (More anxiety gets spent on texting strategy than almost any other part of dating, and nearly all of it is wasted effort. Here is most of what actually matters. Reply in a timeframe you'd be comfortable telling her about. If you wouldn't want to explain your reasoning for waiting three hours, don't do it as a tactic. Reply when it's natural for you to reply busy, then a bit later; free, then soon after. Match effort, roughly. If she's sending short replies, don't send paragraphs and vice versa. Wildly mismatched effort in either direction tends to create pressure. Say things worth responding to. A specific question, a genuine observation, or a real update gives her something to reply to. "Hey" and "what's up" give her nothing to work with. Move toward plans, not just chat. Texting that never turns into meeting .)
/Pg 68 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
