<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 576 0 R
/E (Social media has changed the surface of dating without changing the substance. A few practical notes for navigating it well. A like or a comment is a low-stakes, low-pressure way to show interests appropriate for early stages, before you know each other. Repeated, intense engagement on someone's posts before you've had a real conversation can read as more intense than intended. Your own profile is part of the first impression. It doesn't need to be curated to perfection, but photos that show a real, varied life , friends, activities, genuine smiles  tend to represent you more accurately, and accuracy is the goal, not a highlight reel. Don't let a screen replace real presence. Online interest that never becomes an in-person plan tends to fade. Use social media to build toward meeting, not as a substitute for it.)
/Pg 69 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
