1160 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 586 0 R
/E (This is the shortest chapter in the book because it's the least negotiable one. Every step in dating and physical intimacy  a first kiss, a hand held, anything beyond that  depends on clear, freely given, ongoing agreement from both people. Not agreement extracted through pressure, guilt, alcohol, persistence, or a good mood you're trying to preserve. Agreement that's actually, unambiguously there. A few things follow directly from that: Silence or passivity is not consent. Enthusiasm, or at minimum clear willingness, is the standard  not the absence of a "no." Consent to one thing isn't consent to everything, and it isn't permanent. Someone can want a date and not a kiss, want a kiss and not want to go further, and change their mind at any point without needing to justify it.)
/Pg 79 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
