/E (Everything so far has focused on getting a relationship started. This short chapter is about what actually keeps one going, because attraction that fades in a month was never the goal. Relationship researcher John Gottman's decades of observational work point to a consistent pattern: couples who last aren't the ones who never disagree. They're the ones who maintain what he calls a culture of appreciation and respect ,noticing and naming the good in each other regularly, and repairing the habits conflict quickly rather than letting resentment sit.)
/Pg 81 0 R
/K [1]
>>
