<<
/Title (Once the built-in social structure of school disappears, dating gets logistically harder even as it \(usually\) gets emotionally easier ? you generally know yourself better, and you're less likely to be swept up by every passing crush. You have to build the funnel yourself now. Without classes and dorms doing it for you, meeting people takes deliberate effort: apps, but also hobbies, sports leagues, classes you take for their own sake, friends of friends. Treat this the way you'd treat any other goal worth having  with consistent, unglamorous effort, not a single big push. Apps reward the same fundamentals, expressed differently. A profile that's specific and genuine outperforms one that's trying to seem impressive. Messages  her profile outperform generic openers by a using wit.)
/Dest [85 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4160 0 R
/Next 4176 0 R
>>
