/Title (Being introduced to the people who matter to her is a sign of real trust, and it's worth treating it that way  with genuine effort, not performance. Show real interest in her friends as people, not as an audience to win over. Be yourself, not a more polished version calibrated for approval ? friends and family tend to notice performance faster than she will, precisely because they aren't as emotionally invested in giving you the bene? fit of the doubt. Basic courtesy  remembering names, asking real questions, helping with small things  goes further than any attempt to be impressive.)
