4298 0 obj
<<
/Title (Appearance matters. Anyone who tells you it doesn't is being kind rather than honest. But it matters in a much narrower way than most men think, and misunderstanding that narrowness is where a lot of wasted effort and misplaced insecurity comes from. Here's the more accurate version: appearance is a filter, not a foundation. It affects whether someone is open to a first conversation. It has almost no bearing on whether that conversation turns into genuine interest, and essentially none on whether a relationship lasts. In the mate-preference research discussed in Chapter Two, physical attractiveness took up a real but secondary share of the "budget" people spent on an ideal partner ? consistently smaller than kindness, and roughly on par with other single traits like humor or ambition. That's the honest scale: appearance opens the door. It does not furnish the house.)
/Dest [46 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4294 0 R
/Next 4299 0 R
>>
endobj
