4310 0 obj
<<
/Title (Of everything in this book, effort might be the single most underrated variable, because it's boring to talk about and hard to fake. That second part is exactly why it works. Effort is legible. A woman may not be able to tell whether your charm is genuine in the first ten minutes of meeting you, but she can absolutely tell whether you remembered what she said last week, whether you showed up on time, whether you actually planned something instead of defaulting to "whatever you want to do." Effort is one of the few signals that's expensive to fake, which is exactly why it functions as reliable evidence of real interest, in a way that words alone don't.)
/Dest [48 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4307 0 R
>>
endobj
